// #625 — a diagnostic must name the line its token is really on, even when an
// earlier dead assignment made the lint seek the reporting cursor backwards.
//
// `track_write` reports "Dead assignment" at the PREVIOUS write, which means
// seeking the shared reporting cursor back to it.  `Lexer::to` moves only that
// cursor, so leaving it there shifted every later diagnostic in the file back by
// the seek distance — and each further reassignment stacked another shift.  Two
// dead writes below, so pre-fix the `printt` error was reported two lines early.
//
// The two "Dead assignment" warnings are part of the lock: they must point at
// lines 16 and 17 (the writes that are overwritten), not at a drifted position.
fn helper() -> integer {
  42
}
fn main() {
  c = 1;
  c = 2;
  c = helper();
  printt("x");
  print("c={c}");
}
